WEBVTT

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.520
This is the weather forecast for the
Tokyo area, as released at 1 PM...

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.750
...by the Meteorological Agency's
Forecasting Department.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:13.630
As of 11 AM on the 21st, the large
and powerful Typhoon 32...

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.640
...was in the southernmost parts
of Shizuoka Prefecture...

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.900
...heading northeast
at speeds of 45kph.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.410
Everyone is advised to
use extreme caution...

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.300
Its winds are presently in
the 54kph range...

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.970
...and caution is advised for the
Tokyo Metropolitan Area...

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:18.060
<i>Let's chase our dreams...</i>

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.270
<i>... holding hearts burning...</i>

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.670
<i>... like the summer sunshine.</i>

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.610
<i>If we have courage...</i>

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.770
<i>... at 100 miles an hour...</i>

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:42.880
<i>... I'm sure the door will open.</i>

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:50.030
<i>Since sadness is the road</i>
<i>that leads to smiles...</i>

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:58.740
<i>... dull, dingy shoes will</i>
<i>start to shine, too.</i>

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:05.440
<i>The most wonderful dream</i>
<i>in the world...</i>

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:12.080
<i>The pounding beat speeds up.</i>

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:19.250
<i>The eyes are prisms that</i>
<i>catch the wind...</i>

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:27.170
<i>... and in the voices of</i>
<i>countless friends...</i>

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:34.000
<i>... I feel happiness.</i>

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.380
FILE. 2
TOKYO TYPHOON RALLY

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:52.820
Oh, man, I've had it. It's been
like this every week this year.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.690
Nothing we can do about it. We're up
against Mother Nature, after all.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.300
Oooh! This summer I was sure I was
gonna lose a little more weight...

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.270
...take on a 1-kg parfait, heft the
Sumida Festival palanquin...

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.530
...and at the night stalls, buy apple candy
and fried octopus balls in seaweed...

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.070
...and baked corn and
fresh radish pickles...

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.660
...and go goldfish-catching and balloon
dart-throwing and target shooting...

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.740
...and shelltops... and then, uh,
brown sugar candy, oh, hey!

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.830
Okay, okay. We're moving.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:17.310
Aw, there's no point
to anything now...

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.980
Hmh? Miyuki, pull
over to the left.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.990
Huh? Okay...

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.720
Students of Wakaba Preschool, please
go straight home immediately.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:30.030
Don't go anywhere else. There's
a scary typhoon on the way.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:33.330
Wow! It's Natsumi!
It's Miyuki!

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.560
Hey!

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.600
What's with this "Natsumi" stuff?
That's "Miss Natsumi" to you!

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.800
Well, your name is
Natsumi, right?

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.000
Ri-ight?

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.940
It's enough for us to call
you Natsumi, right?

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:44.740
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:48.280
Hey, hey, Miyuki, do you know where
there's an animal hospital?

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:52.480
Huh? A vet? I'm not sure if
there is one in this area...

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.420
You don't even know that?

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:57.150
Some policewoman
you are.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:03.000
"...Preschool"

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.690
Huh? Isn't that Chibi?
You sure got big.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.600
Do you know this
cat, Natsumi?

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.760
Hey, how do you know?
Huh?

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:18.680
There is nothing that Natsumi the hero
doesn't know. Are you impressed?

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.580
You can't
fool us with that.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.780
Don't
belittle the masses!

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.450
What's going on? Are you
keeping her, Maho?

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.220
Uh-uh. She came to the preschool
a little while ago.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:34.230
She's not feeling well. She
doesn't eat anything.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.290
So that's why you wanted to take
her to the hospital, huh?

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:37.990
Uh-huh.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.600
I get it now.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:40.860
Oh, it's Ken!

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.840
Kennie's here! Kennie's here!
Kennie's on his motorcycle!

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.170
Kennie! Kennie! Kennie!

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.710
Oh, so Nakajima is "Kennie"
around here?

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:52.850
Sort of...

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.410
What's this? She's
awfully fat...

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.450
Stop that! You've got
to hold her properly.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.130
Oh, uh, I see...

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:05.990
All right, we'll see that
she's taken care of.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.090
Will she be okay?

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:12.330
We'll take care of it. We promise.
So you all hurry home. Go on!

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:21.970
Look out!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.480
Hey! Where'd you learn to drive?! Don't
mess around like that, you idiot!

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:32.020
Natsumi's scary!

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:35.080
That Lancia... it's
got to be!

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:37.220
Umm... Nakajima...

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:50.800
I'm now going to catch
that ill-mannered car!

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.100
So take care, everyone!

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.840
Oh, he fell over!

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.980
That GSX...

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:21.100
I see, I see. I knew it all the time,
uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:25.330
Oh, cut it out, Natsumi. You're
just jeering at us both.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.960
You're no better than
those preschoolers.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.440
Thanks to whom, we blew our
chance to catch that Lancia!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:34.810
Well, well, nice change of subject.
Won't work on me, though.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:36.940
Natsumi!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.420
Welcome back!

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.650
You're done for the day, right?

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.480
Yeah. We've done
our nightshift.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.990
Hey, hey, Nakajima's looking
a little funny.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.320
You know anything
about it?

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.520
Oh! Not you too, Yoriko!

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.030
Something DID happen,
didn't it!

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.330
It sure did!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:10.480
I guess this will do for now.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.850
But you know, Nakajima
didn't look at all happy.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.790
He just went and locked
himself in the morgue.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.450
I bet he was just blushing.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:20.650
Oh!

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.920
Are you gonna have kittens?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:23.860
Eh?!

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.690
Oh, yeah! Her breasts are big!

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.560
That's why she's so listless!

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.430
So that's it!

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.700
Kobayakawa!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.700
I need to ask you something.
Please come!

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:37.180
Uh... Okay.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.180
Hey, hey, "something
to ask" must be!

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.750
A proposal. It's got to be!

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.510
Who'd have thought they'd
have gotten that close!

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.660
It's a big scoop.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:48.690
We're tagging along, right?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.380
Oh, let's.

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.390
All right!

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:04.800
The rain's pouring down so loud, I can't
hear what they're talking about at all.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.600
Who cares what they're talking about?
It's actions that matter!

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.370
Go! Go get 'er, Nakajima!

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:13.740
You're the only one I can
ask this of. I beg you!

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.750
For something like that,
I'll gladly assist you.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:21.480
And besides, there are a couple others
who look like they'll help... right?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:42.000
Natsumi! Bring that toolbox!

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.470
Uh, right!

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:47.210
Yoriko! There's an auxiliary flashing
light and radio! Bring them here!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:47.920
Uh, right!

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.620
Uh, right!
Natsumi, I need a speaker too!

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:49.750
Natsumi, I need a speaker too!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:50.790
Huh? Where is it?

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.220
On the highest shelf in the back!

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.520
Okay, here you go.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:55.660
Now get me some grease.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.630
Uh, right, right!
Now get me some grease.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.700
I'm pooped.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:03.560
Hey!

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.330
Eh?

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.690
Thanks.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.500
Thanks for doing
this all for me...

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:12.110
Uh-uh, no problem. I can't do
anything useful anyway...

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.870
But I'm a little disappointed,
you know?

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:20.140
So this is what your request turned
out to be? Oh, and we were sure...

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.940
Huh? What did you
think it was?

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:25.380
Eh? Uh, well, um...
Never mind that.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:28.150
Are you really going to go out there
using a..."KLE," was it...

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.420
...as a police motorcycle?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:33.390
Even you wouldn't stand a chance in
the middle of a typhoon like this.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:37.400
I know it's risky. I have
my reasons...

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.290
What condition are
the victims in?

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:05.860
I don't know, but the ambulance
should already be on its way.

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:09.050
Tell Nakajima that the
bike's finished.

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:10.720
And see that the cat gets fed.

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:12.200
Cat food and water, right?

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.930
I used to enjoy typhoons,
you know?

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:53.900
Now we can't just enjoy
them, can we?

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:07.150
Mini Patrol Four calling Bokuto Station!
How long before the ambulance arrives?

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:10.950
Well... the roads are badly flooded,
and it seems to be taking a detour.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.150
Looks like it'll take another
ten minutes or so.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.390
Roger! We'll figure something
out! Miyuki!

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:16.530
I know!

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.440
It's gonna be all right now.
Natsumi! Hurry!

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:26.660
It's locked! Hang on a sec!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.200
Wha?!

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.070
Now that it's come to this...

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:37.280
...we can only exercise
brute force!

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:39.820
Here we go...

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.860
DIAMOND KNUCKLE ATTACK!

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:44.890
I'm through.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:48.650
Oh wow!

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.040
The watermelons are
all taken care of.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.200
Nice going. Here.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.350
Thanks.

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:13.090
So what was the cause?

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.220
Well, you see...

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.290
A Lancia Delta? Then the
one this afternoon?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.760
Probably... in which case, it's
just as Nakajima feared...

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.860
Eh? What does "Kennie"
have to do with it? Ow...

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:31.400
It seems it appears every year at this
time, only on days with typhoons...

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:34.740
...a legendary car that runs through
town like it owned the place.

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.840
Then, you mean, a year ago?

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:38.810
Yes... through some
happenstance...

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:42.610
...Nakajima met up with
and challenged it.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.010
And he lost, huh?

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:47.950
The bike was a serious handicap! He
was up against four-wheel drive.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:52.080
And it was outfitted for rallying. Not
even Nakajima could beat that!

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:55.190
So that's why he wanted the KLE 500
with foul-weather outfitting.

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.590
That's Nakajima for you; he doesn't
like to lose, does he?

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:03.130
It's not just that. The Lancia's reckless
driving escalates each year.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:06.040
Fact is, it didn't cause any accidents
up until last year.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.540
If left alone at the rate it's
going, next we'll have...

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.280
Yes, this is Mini Patrol
Four. Go ahead.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:17.780
Natsumi, Miyuki, I don't know
what to do. Hurry back here!

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:38.900
It won't eat, it makes weird high-pitched
cries... It just won't settle down!

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.240
Aren't its kittens about
to be born?

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.140
If so, it wouldn't be crying.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.300
Besides, it looks like
it's in a lot of pain.

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:48.870
I thought of calling a veterinarian,
but there's all the wind and rain...

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:53.180
We can't very well wait for the typhoon
to pass. Natsumi! Get things ready!

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.720
All right! Leave it to me!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.790
Where? Say again!

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.700
Saitoo Animal Hospital, 7-4
Morishita-cho, Sumida-ku.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:12.740
They stop examining patients at five,
but they said they'd have a look.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:13.870
Roger.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:23.110
Animal hospital? What
are those two up to?

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.970
This is Bokuto Station.
Go ahead.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:53.810
Yoriko? What are Kobayakawa
and Tsujimoto doing?

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.140
Oh, Nakajima, you see...

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:58.110
Blackout!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.280
People will start mobbing the phone
lines. Get someone on it!

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:01.460
The circuit's holding!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.320
The circuit's holding!
Hey! Yoriko!

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:38.120
Looks like a breech birth. On top of
which, her pelvis seems narrow.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.280
Well, what do we do?

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.820
I'm sorry, but with things the
way they are right now...

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:46.790
Not much you can do in
a blackout, is there?

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:50.460
Let me see if I can contact the
Veterinarians' Association.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:52.370
I think there'll be a place somewhere
that will take her in.

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:55.370
Please!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:02.370
We didn't hear anything about a blackout.
Tell us these things ahead of time!

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:07.350
Sorry. But things were all messed up
here, too. They still are, though...

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:11.120
Where was that hospital
the vet referred us to?

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:14.650
Ayase, in Adachi-ku. We can work it out
if we get to the Kosuge Interchange.

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:18.100
Oh, Capital Expressway Six is
closed due to construction!

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:22.500
Why you! You should tell us
things like that beforehand!

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:25.570
Aww, it happened
three days ago!

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:28.770
If it's closed, that means no
one's driving on it... right?

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.010
Is... that so?!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:35.870
Mini Patrol Four is now en route to Ayase.
We will be taking Capital Expressway Six!

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.810
What! Are you serious? That's...

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.680
Over and out! So long!

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.890
"ENTRANCE"

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:49.220
"NO TRESPASSING"
"Bokuto Police Station"

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:53.260
The wind's really hellacious!

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:55.230
Feels like we're gonna
get swept away!

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:59.430
Driving in this rain and crosswind
is a life-threatening proposition.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.010
If you're getting out, do it now.

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:04.630
Looking to get it all to yourself?
That's not fair.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.650
This is where the fun begins.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.010
Roger!

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.430
We're almost there. Hang on!

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:31.800
What's this?

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:33.460
What do you mean?

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:37.810
I thought it was a little bit strange, to see
such a gentle expression on your face.

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.700
What're you talking about?

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:44.810
It's much stranger for you to be doing
something this outrageous!

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:47.320
That makes us even, huh?

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:49.360
What is it?

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:50.250
There's a car behind us!

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:51.850
No way! Huh!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.030
What the?! It's that Lancia Delta!

00:17:59.030 --> 00:17:59.760
I know!

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.760
Of all the times it could
pick to show up!

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:04.230
He's not likely to let us
go by quietly, is he?

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:18.040
He's out of his mind! Miyuki, blow
him away with the nitro!

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.420
That's impossible in
these conditions!

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.960
It's too dangerous with this wind
and this poor visibility!

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.180
Besides...

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:28.890
Oh, yeah. There's no telling
whether Chibi could take it.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:47.450
Miyuki! Get off at Tsutsumi Avenue!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:48.110
Huh?

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:50.270
Let the Lancia Delta
pass us by.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.150
At this rate, he'll mess
you up, Miyuki!

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:54.980
Even if he follows us, we'll have the edge
down below. We'll figure something out.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.120
You're right.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.360
He's got us figured! He's
not going to let us off!

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.500
Goddamn!

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:14.470
He's a little better than I am.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:15.840
Miyuki...

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:19.170
What do we do?

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.640
Mini Patrol Four, do
you read me?

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.080
Nakajima?!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.150
Where are you, Nakajima?!

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:27.650
Right in front of you.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:35.020
Yoriko filled me in.

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:36.860
You're carrying a patient, so you must
be having a hard time fighting him.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.120
I'll back you up.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.070
Kennie! You're so cool!

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.030
Stop that.

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:49.130
I'm the one who's taking you
on! Come and get me!

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:56.480
Kobayakawa! It's only
5 km to Kosuge!

00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:00.210
Get into his slipstream and follow us!
His car should act as a windbreak!

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:03.550
Will you be all right, Nakajima? Bikes are
the most dangerous in this weather!

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:07.450
I put my faith in this bike
you tuned, Kobayakawa.

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:43.530
Oh, man! We've already reached
the Kosuge offramp!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.960
Hey, hey, Miyuki, you've fallen for
"Kennie" all over again, I bet.

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:49.970
Look, I told you to stop referring
to him like that.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.300
Well, how about Kenbo? Ken-Ken?
Kensuke? The Kenster?

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.430
"Kennie" really is best,
don't you think?

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.030
Oh! It's from "Kennie!"

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.200
This is where we
part for now.

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:02.680
I'll join you after I take
care of this clown.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.750
Take care of that
chubby Chibi.

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:13.290
I wonder if he can win out.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:16.260
Sure he can! He will! Kennie
can if anyone can!

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:21.460
Natsumi! You keep saying, "Kennie,
Kennie," and now I'm doing it, too...

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:24.930
What's wrong with that? You're gonna
be calling him that sooner or later!

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:28.200
How can you say that! Don't decide
such things by yourself!

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:31.140
Whatever! Keep your
eyes on the road!

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:32.050
Don't try to evade the subject!

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:34.100
We're gonna crash!

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:41.650
I repeat...

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:46.120
...the Joban Line is currently halted
within the Tokyo city limits.

00:21:47.690 --> 00:21:53.190
It is unclear when service
will be reestablished.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:09.510
Right at the next corner. Then
left about 300m after that!

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:10.580
Roger!

00:22:14.050 --> 00:22:15.920
Hang in there! It's just
a little longer!

00:22:19.890 --> 00:22:21.860
You bastard!

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:25.830
Ah-ah!

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:33.530
I'm not like I was last year!

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:43.470
We can't get through here!
Where's a detour?

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:48.850
Hold on... Back up and go left on that last
road... no good! Neither is going right!

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:49.990
Which way?

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:51.990
Which way?
Mmm... there is no way.

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:52.060
Mmm... there is no way.

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:53.290
Eh?! It can't be!
Mmm... there is no way.

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:56.990
With this much water, it's all the same
no matter which way you go!

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:59.690
Getting around this will mean
going way out of our way.

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:04.200
Which means we only have one option
left... Natsumi, you're on!

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:06.430
I had a feeling it would
come to this.

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:14.480
All set. Natsumi, this
is the final hurdle.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:18.320
No problem. My bike technique
can stand up to this typhoon!

00:23:19.190 --> 00:23:20.150
Yeah!

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:24.260
Go!

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:04.550
I've got something to say
to you. Listen up!

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:07.130
When driving near children,
maintain a safe distance...

00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:10.200
...and furthermore, go slowly!
Remember that.

00:24:31.630 --> 00:24:34.860
"Animal Hospital"

00:25:18.810 --> 00:25:22.100
"This is a present for good children.
Pick it up gently."

00:25:55.610 --> 00:25:58.440
"Miss Natsumi, Miss Miyuki,
Thank You"

00:26:28.740 --> 00:26:37.080
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

00:26:37.150 --> 00:26:46.490
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:54.500
<i>The sunset skyline flashes past</i>
<i>in my side-view mirror.</i>

00:26:54.570 --> 00:27:02.060
<i>This is the road I drive on every day,</i>
<i>believing in my dreams.</i>

00:27:02.180 --> 00:27:09.980
<i>On rainy days, windy days, and days</i>
<i>when I wanted to throw it all away...</i>

00:27:10.080 --> 00:27:17.750
<i>... you smiled as you</i>
<i>sat beside me.</i>

00:27:19.030 --> 00:27:23.530
<i>I love the unchanging vista, the sky</i>
<i>that we watch together.</i>

00:27:27.530 --> 00:27:34.340
<i>That's why I'm confident that I can</i>
<i>hang in there, if it's for you.</i>

00:27:34.410 --> 00:27:42.810
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

00:27:42.920 --> 00:27:43.050
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

00:27:49.390 --> 00:27:49.420
<i>I love this town where we</i>
<i>happened to meet...</i>

00:27:52.930 --> 00:27:57.230
Honestly, those kids... Miyuki,
this isn't coming off!

00:27:57.400 --> 00:27:59.560
Look, just put some elbow
grease into it.

00:27:59.670 --> 00:28:01.430
We'll clean her up even
if it takes all day.

00:28:01.600 --> 00:28:04.970
Eek! No way!

00:28:06.810 --> 00:28:09.080
"THE TRUTH BEHIND
THE RUMORS"

00:28:09.080 --> 00:28:12.480
Why are you having a matchmaking, when
you have someone like Nakajima?

00:28:12.980 --> 00:28:13.510
Want me to tell?

00:28:13.510 --> 00:28:16.110
Want me to tell?
Hey, who are you talking about?

00:28:16.280 --> 00:28:19.250
Stop her, Nakajima! You're the
only one who can stop Miyuki!

00:28:19.420 --> 00:28:21.110
Look, what are you
talking about?

00:28:21.290 --> 00:28:21.950
Wanna know?

00:28:22.120 --> 00:28:24.610
You want her to be taken away by
some nobody from nowhere?

00:28:24.790 --> 00:28:26.850
How did you come up
with a story like that?

00:28:27.030 --> 00:28:28.050
Shall I tell you?

00:28:28.230 --> 00:28:29.990
So you're the cause of all this!

00:28:30.160 --> 00:28:33.460
You're Under Arrest, File 3,
"Love's Highway Stars."

00:28:33.630 --> 00:28:36.800
FILE. 3
LOVE'S HIGHWAY STARS
